---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import ActionMatcher from "../components/ui/ActionMatcher.astro";
import Button from "../components/ui/Button.astro";
import Callout from "../components/ui/Callout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/ui/Hero.astro";
import LadderRung from "../components/ui/LadderRung.astro";
import Section from "../components/ui/Section.astro";
import Signature from "../components/ui/Signature.astro";
import Stitch from "../components/ui/Stitch.astro";

// TODO(Action Network): every rung below uses a mailto: fallback because the
// organization's Action Network account doesn't exist yet. Once it does
// (signup form, petition, state-legislator letter campaign — see README's
// Action Network compliance checklist), swap the marked hrefs for the
// AN-hosted pages with a ?source=<rung> code, and enable the AN widget
// embed here per the plan. Until then, every link on this page must still
// work — a mailto: link that opens the visitor's own email app does.
const email = "join@automate-ethically.com";
---

<Page
	title="Take action | Automate Ethically"
	description="Pick the step you can reach today. Thirty seconds or an hour, every bit of it counts."
	ogImage="/og/act.png"
>
	<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 12: /act framing -->
	<Hero eyebrow="Take action" title="Pick the step you can reach today." titleId="act-title" chips>
		<p class="ae-hero-sub">
			Rules change when neighbors organize. You don't have to do all six of
			these. Even one moves the needle, and none of them cost money or ask you
			to be an expert.
		</p>
	</Hero>

	<Stitch />

	<!-- The same two questions as the home page, filtering the same list. -->
	<Section id="match" wide>
		<ActionMatcher name="act" heading="Start with what fits your week." />
	</Section>

	<Stitch />

	<Section label="Ways to help" wide>
		<Callout tone="warn" title="New here?">
			Start with rung 1. It takes thirty seconds, and you can always come back
			for the rest.
		</Callout>
		<ol class="ae-ladder">
			<LadderRung id="join" time="30 seconds" title="1. Join the list">
				<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 13: rung one-liners -->
				<p>
					We'll email you when there's something happening in your state.
					Nothing more often than that, and never anything asking for money.
				</p>
				<div class="ae-cta-row">
					<Button
						size="sm"
						href={`mailto:${email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Add me to the list")}&body=${encodeURIComponent("My city/town: \nMy state: \n")}`}
					>Join by email</Button>
				</div>
			</LadderRung>

			<LadderRung id="petition" time="2 minutes" title="2. Sign the petition">
				<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 14: petition text -->
				<p>
					"One rule: a human makes the decision, and answers for it."
					Signatures get shown to city councils as proof that people in their
					town care about this. They are not sent to any candidate or party.
				</p>
				<div class="ae-cta-row">
					<Button
						size="sm"
						href={`mailto:${email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Count me in on the petition")}&body=${encodeURIComponent("Name: \nCity/town: \nI support the rule: a human makes the decision, and answers for it.\n")}`}
					>Sign by email</Button>
				</div>
			</LadderRung>

			<LadderRung id="share" time="5 minutes" title="3. Share it">
				<p>
					A broadside was made to be nailed up. Print
					<a href="/toolkit/one-pager">the one-pager</a> and pin it somewhere
					people will actually read it: a corkboard, a laundromat, a library.
					Or just send this page to one neighbor.
				</p>
				<div class="ae-cta-row">
					<Button
						size="sm"
						variant="secondary"
						href={`mailto:?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Thought you'd want to see this")}&body=${encodeURIComponent("https://automate-ethically.com")}`}
					>Email one neighbor</Button>
					<Button size="sm" variant="secondary" href="/toolkit/one-pager">Print it</Button>
				</div>
				<p class="ae-quote-cards-intro">
					Or save one of these and post it wherever you post things:
				</p>
				<div class="ae-quote-cards">
					<a href="/og/quote-principle.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
						<img src="/og/quote-principle.png" alt="A human should make the decision." loading="lazy" />
					</a>
					<a href="/og/quote-loom.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
						<img src="/og/quote-loom.png" alt="The loom did not remove the weaver. A person still chose the pattern, punched the cards, examined the cloth, and signed the bolt." loading="lazy" />
					</a>
					<a href="/og/quote-anger.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
						<img src="/og/quote-anger.png" alt="The anger is real. Aim it at the rulebook." loading="lazy" />
					</a>
				</div>
			</LadderRung>

			<LadderRung id="write" time="10 to 20 minutes" title="4. Write to your officials">
				<p>This one's really two smaller tasks, honestly costed:</p>
				<h3 class="ae-rung-sub">Your state representative, about 10 minutes</h3>
				<p>
					They're easy to reach: look up their contact page, then copy the note
					below (in your own words is even better) and paste it in.
				</p>
				<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 15b: this template still reads like a
				     policy memo, not a neighbor's letter. Kai's open dissent
				     (docs/adversarial-review/reviews/2026-08-29-action-ladder-accessibility.md):
				     match the plain, first-person register the rest of the toolkit uses. -->
				<figure class="ae-epigraph">
					<blockquote>
						I'm a neighbor in [your town]. I'm asking you to support a rule:
						when an automated system (a camera network, an algorithm) makes a
						decision that affects someone's life, a named person has to review
						it and be accountable for it. Montana already passed this for state
						agencies (HB 178). I'd like to see it here too. Thank you for
						reading this.
					</blockquote>
				</figure>
				<h3 class="ae-rung-sub">Your city council, 15 to 20 minutes, longer the first time</h3>
				<p>
					We can't look up your city council for you. You know your town better
					than we do. This part takes longer because you'll need to find their
					contact info yourself.
				</p>
				<div class="ae-cta-row">
					<Button size="sm" variant="secondary" href="/toolkit/find-your-council">Find your council</Button>
				</div>
			</LadderRung>

			<LadderRung id="speak" time="1 hour" title="5. Show up and speak">
				<p>
					This is the one that actually moves an ordinance. Most council
					meetings pass with almost nobody in the room, so a handful of
					neighbors speaking on the same issue stands out.
				</p>
				<div class="ae-cta-row">
					<Button size="sm" href="/toolkit/council-script">Get the 2-minute script</Button>
					<Button size="sm" variant="secondary" href="/toolkit/find-your-council">Find your meeting</Button>
				</div>
			</LadderRung>

			<LadderRung id="lead" time="ongoing" title="6. Become a local lead">
				<p>
					If you're willing to be the person your town calls on this, whether
					that means hosting a meeting, tracking the council's agenda, or just
					being a point of contact, tell us what's happening where you live.
				</p>
				<Signature name="A person, by name.">
					Becoming a local lead means your name is on your town's page, and you
					answer for it.
				</Signature>
				<div class="ae-cta-row">
					<Button
						size="sm"
						href={`mailto:${email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent("I want to help organize locally")}&body=${encodeURIComponent("My city/town: \nWhat's happening there: \nWhat I can help with (host a meeting / track the agenda / speak / something else): \n")}`}
					>Tell us about your town</Button>
				</div>
			</LadderRung>
		</ol>
	</Section>
</Page>

<style>
	/* The ladder rungs carry their own frame, so this is only the stack. */
	.ae-ladder {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 2rem 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 18px;
	}
</style>
